    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0372" n="284" xml:id="pg284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/3116</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Italian Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Valentino</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-01-22">January 22,
                            1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your Note of November 19, 1918, transmitting a memorandum regarding
                    the situation in Tripoli arising out of the reported violation of the armistice
                    by Turkey, and stating that the Italian Government would appreciate it if the
                    American Government would approach the British Government with the view of
                    having Turkey keep faith to her engagements.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform you that as the United States is not at war
                    with Turkey and is not a party to the armistice it is unable to take the
                    requested action in this matter.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
